  Quote of the Week:

  Pope Julius II, in reply to Michelangelo, who had asked which of his 
artistic tools the Pope would like to try (1506):
  "Nay, give me a sword, for I am no scholar."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  In spring, Catilina prepared her armies to defend Poland and the 
surrounding provinces.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Catilina for this year.



  Here is the financial report for Catilina's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  0 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Catilina was left 
with 34 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Tarsus
To: Catilina

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I prepared my armies to defend Italy and the surrounding 
provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Tarsus


STATE OF THE NATION:

  My lord and sovereign, greatest of Kings, I humbly beg thy leave to make
